- Usage is billed in vCPU minutes: Each instance shape has a vCPU count, and usage is calculated as that count multiplied by job runtime in minutes, measured to the second. Startup and shutdown periods are excluded, with no minimum charges. You can view your vCPU minute consumption on the Usage page in your Buildkite organization, which shows vCPU minutes by default with a toggle to switch to job minutes by instance shape.
- Caching is included at no additional cost: There are no supplementary charges for storage or cache usage. Cache volumes operate on high-speed, local NVMe-attached disks, substantially accelerating caching and disk operations. This results in faster job completion, reduced minute consumption, and lower overall costs.
...
- Transparent remote Docker builders at no additional cost: Offloading Docker build commands to dedicated, pre-configured machines equipped with Docker layer caching and additional performance optimizations. This feature operates without any additional configuration, and is available to Enterprise plan customers only.
...
