Can required status checks for branch protection reference a specific job inside a matrix, or only the workflow as a whole? Deployments Medium

Branch protection's required status checks are set per job name, and a matrix job reports one status check per generated combination, each with the matrix values appended to its name (something like `test (18, ubuntu-latest)`). That means adding a new value to the matrix later, a new Node version, changes the exact check names branch protection is watching for, and a rule configured against the old names can end up waiting on a check that no longer gets produced, silently blocking every merge until someone notices and updates the required checks list.
...
Can a reusable workflow call another reusable workflow? Reusable Workflows Hard

Yes, but GitHub caps the nesting depth, a caller workflow can call reusable workflows up to four levels deep, and a single workflow run can reference up to 20 unique reusable workflows total. In practice this rarely bites anyone until an org tries to build a shared library of composable pipeline stages and starts layering call-a-workflow-that-calls-a-workflow patterns without tracking the depth.

