New10, a Netherlands-based digital financial lender and subsidiary of ABN AMRO Bank N.V., needed a developer-friendly, scalable platform that would let engineers own their code, deploy quickly and safely, and meet strict banking security and privacy requirements. GitLab Ultimate gave New10 a single platform for source code management and CI/CD, helping the startup avoid context switching while supporting its modern cloud-native architecture.

With GitLab, New10 implemented integrated version control, CI/CD, security scanning, and AWS/Kubernetes support, including runners hosted on Kubernetes for testing and QA. The results were significant: deployment speed improved by 3x, release frequency increased from twice per month to twice per day, and security feedback loops shortened so issues could be fixed before deployment.

