A computer science or related degree signals sustained commitment, foundational theory (algorithms, math, systems), and — rightly or not — passes an initial resume filter at companies that screen by degree before looking at anything else. It takes 3-4 years and a large upfront cost, and the curriculum is rarely current with fast-moving AI tools.

An AI certification or short course signals that you've recently, deliberately built a specific skill set — but only if it's backed by real projects. A certificate with no portfolio behind it is close to worthless in Indian AI hiring today; the market has been flooded with certificate-only candidates, and experienced interviewers know to ask "show me what you built," not "what does your certificate say."

