In its traditional motion, Knife River argued that promissory estoppel is not an independent cause of action in Texas in an employment context. We agree. Promissory estoppel is an equitable exception used to avoid a statute of frauds defense. “Moore” Burger, Inc. v. Phillips Petroleum Co., Citator data locked 492 S.W.2d 934, 936 (Tex.1973). It is a defensive plea that does not create a contract where none existed before, but rather prevents a party from insisting upon its strict legal rights under the statute of frauds when enforcing a non-compliant agreement would be necessary to avoid an injustice. See Hruska v. First State Bank, Citator data locked 747 S.W.2d 783, 785 (Tex.1988); Id.

